{
  "slug": "project:cosmic-the-original--daniele-baldelli",
  "name": "Cosmic - The Original",
  "editorial_article": "Released in 2007 as a double-disc compilation, Cosmic - The Original 1979–1984 curates the specific, hypnotic selection of records popularized by Daniele Baldelli at the Italian club Cosmic. The set captures the atmosphere of his residencies in Lazise, where Baldelli pioneered a style mixing funk, electro, jazz fusion, and Brazilian music at deliberately adjusted speeds. He frequently played 45 RPM records at 33 RPM, or vice versa, to force tracks into a 90–110 BPM range, creating a psychedelic and churning soundscape. This collection documents the era where Baldelli utilized flangers and equalizers to transform textures, often layering percussive African tracks over electronic compositions to build his unique mix of tribal and mechanical sound. The compilation remains a primary archival reference for the influence of the Northern Italian 'cosmic sound' on modern space disco.",
